
                                                 MEMDELETE COMMAND


Deletes a range of data.

Below is the syntax :
                                         memDelete 	-from address  -l len 

---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES       |    DESCRIPTION
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -from       |    Address from which data should be deleted. Mandatory switch.
   -l          |    Specifies length of data to be deleted. Mandatory switch.
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Example:
	read -in input1.hex
	memDelete -addr 0x80801000 -l 0x10
	write -out outputFile.hex -lyt 0x10
	
